          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"The expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. His immediately preceding thought explicitly frames it as something he believes, although the narration also emphasizes that he uses the conventional words expected on such an occasion.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"да и я люблю ее\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.82,\"reason\":\"In this engagement setting, the avowal weakly confirms or invokes the newly established romantic relationship, but it does not itself clearly propose marriage, promise fidelity, or specify another undertaking. Pierre is already described as holding his fiancée's hand before he says it, so the surrounding engagement should not be transferred wholesale onto the target.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The words are not represented as a reflex-like affective outburst. Pierre pauses, deliberates about what convention requires, and recalls the expected formula; their poor sound and his shame further mark them as controlled speech rather than expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"No core force beyond the avowal and its weak relationship-confirming implication is needed. The expression's awkward, socially scripted quality affects its interpretation and sincerity evidence but is not a separate speech-act mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been treated by their assembled family and guests as newly engaged, despite Pierre's hesitation. After they are left alone, Hélène initiates a kiss. Pierre then remembers the conventional words expected in such a situation and tells her, “Je vous aime,” feeling ashamed at how poorly they sound.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target itself contains no explicit promise or proposal. At most, Pierre weakly ratifies the romantic relationship that others have already declared established. Hélène's preceding kiss supports interpersonal uptake of the courtship situation, while the later marriage shows that the engagement proceeded; neither establishes that this particular avowal independently undertook marriage. Pierre's attraction and self-attributed love support affection, but his dread, shame, passivity, and reliance on a scripted formula complicate sincerity and the nature of that affection.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied text is recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification relies only on the supplied blocks.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence gives substantial access to Pierre's thoughts but little direct access to Hélène's inner state. It therefore cannot fully settle her emotional uptake or the sincerity and durability of Pierre's love beyond this represented moment.\"}"
        }
